# Production build env — loaded automatically by `vite build`.
#
# Vite loads .env first, then this file OVERRIDES any duplicate keys. We use
# that to force secrets to empty strings in the production bundle, while
# letting non-secret values (Firebase web config) flow through from .env.
#
# Why empty strings work: the loaders in src/ use the pattern
#   localStorage.getItem(...) ?? import.meta.env.VITE_... ?? ''
# so a blank value here forces each user to enter their own credentials via
# the app's Settings tab (stored in their browser's localStorage).
#
# Firebase config is intentionally NOT listed here — those values are public
# (access is gated by firestore.rules) and inherit from .env at build time.
# If you deploy from CI without .env, inject the VITE_FIREBASE_* vars via
# your CI secrets instead.
#
# Verify after `npm run build`:
#   grep -r "sk-ant-\|ghp_\|github_pat_" dist/   # should print nothing

# --- GitHub default repo (per-user OAuth handled via Sign in with GitHub) ---
VITE_GITHUB_OWNER=
VITE_GITHUB_REPO=

# --- Anthropic / Claude Managed Agents (per-user — keep empty in production) ---
# The Anthropic API key lives in Secret Manager, not in the bundle.
VITE_ANTHROPIC_AGENT_ID=
VITE_ANTHROPIC_ENV_ID=
VITE_ANTHROPIC_VAULT_ID=
